# Design: Windows foundation source compile

## 概述

Pure core restoration is separate from management.

## 技术方案
Management checkout D6+7 is distinct from RUNNER_TEMP fresh SUT. Python guard fetches only fixed immutable backup commits in Eswink/coding-tools-mcp, reads exact73 inert .source bytes, verifies embedded finite manifest, restores original modes to custom native Git index, and applies SHA-bound full43 patch. Native write-tree/count checks d4/1913 then19bb/1953. Every tracked blob and executable mode is checked in materialized SUT before and after commands.

## Requirement Mapping
FR-1: fixed source manifest and native Git reconstruction; FR-2: fixed Actions jobs and PowerShell commands; FR-3: no native flags or native_source compilation constant, immutable positive SHA, fixed refs; FR-4: isolated local payload mode plus tamper cases, separate source receipts.

## Interfaces
Python restore --manifest --destination --receipt accepts --local-payload for reproducible local guard tests or immutable public backup Git source on CI. Python verify --manifest --destination --receipt compares full pure tree worktree. No command or source input from workflow_dispatch. PowerShell takes only fixed management path and runner temp, runs fixed cargo commands, preserving every result. Linux Go command is explicit data-only files.

## Failure Handling
A wrong source, patch SHA, tree/count/path/mode/protected positive denies compiler. Compiler nonzero stops data tests but always saves receipts/artifacts. Tests must discover nonzero matching cases, and source guards repeat even after failures. No parser result substitutes types or native outcomes.

## Security and Constraints
contents read, persist-credentials false, no secrets/native fixture flags. Original16assert positive is never run/skipped/edited. PR98 cancelled10 and snapshot pause bytes remain exact. New foundation is replacement source, not recovery of missing historical40. Whole Rust build may fail; preserve failure rather than treating historical runs as present success.

## 文件结构

- .github/workflows/windows-foundation-source-compile.yml
- scripts/windows_foundation_source_compile.ps1
- scripts/windows_foundation_source_guard.py
- scripts/windows_foundation_source_manifest.json
- docs/specs/windows-foundation-source-compile/requirements.md
- docs/specs/windows-foundation-source-compile/design.md
- docs/specs/windows-foundation-source-compile/tasks.md

## Frozen02 runtime and management closure
PS calls the resolved executable source rather than searching PATH again, records Git before any Python restoration, resolves Rust1.98.1 actual rustc/cargo payload through rustup which, invokes their canonical payload paths and confirms both paths and hashes after. Python manager verifier compares HEAD==GITHUB_SHA and seven native HEAD blob/mode identities with actual file bytes. It runs before and after compiler, separately from1953SUT checks. Git child environment clears caller GIT_* options, uses empty global/system configs, disabled hooks and object replacement; approved backup commits/prefixes are literals.

Cargo uses the actual resolved RUSTC payload explicitly; inherited compiler/wrapper overrides are refused and both wrapper config fields explicitly empty. CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 excludes incremental reuse. Primary Cargo environment documentation explicitly defines RUSTC and wrapper behavior; this is compiler provenance, not permission.
